===
# Class Attributes

CSS classes for Reveal.js and custom styling

===
# Pure Class Attribute

::: {.r-fit-text}
## This Text Will Fit Container
Using Reveal.js built-in class
:::

===
# Multiple Classes

::: {.fragment .fade-in}
This will fade in as a fragment when you advance
:::

::: {.fragment .fade-out}
This will fade out
:::

===
# Class with Inline Styles

::: {.r-stretch; background: '#3498db'; padding: '20px'; color: 'white'}
## Stretched Content
Combined Reveal.js class with custom styles
:::

===
# Custom Classes

::: {.my-custom-class; background: '#2ecc71'; color: 'white'; padding: '25px'; border-radius: '10px'}
### Custom Styled Box
You can add your own class names for custom CSS
:::

===
# Reveal.js Fragment Classes

::: {.fragment .highlight-red}
This fragment will be highlighted in red
:::

::: {.fragment .highlight-blue}
This fragment will be highlighted in blue
:::

::: {.fragment .highlight-green}
This fragment will be highlighted in green
:::

===
# Multiple Custom Classes

::: {.box .shadow .rounded; padding: '20px'}
### Multiple Classes Applied
- box
- shadow
- rounded

(Add corresponding CSS in your theme)
:::

===
# Class Names with Hyphens

::: {.my-special-box; background: '#9b59b6'; color: 'white'; padding: '20px'}
### Hyphenated Class Name
Classes with hyphens work perfectly
:::

===
# Class Names with Underscores

::: {.my_underscore_class; background: '#e67e22'; color: 'white'; padding: '20px'}
### Underscored Class Name
Classes with underscores also work
:::

